<main id="main-doc">

  <section class="main-section" id="HTML_Basics">
    <header>HTML Basics</header>

    <p>HTML is the standard language used to create the structure of web pages.</p>
    <p>HTML elements describe content such as headings, paragraphs, images, and links.</p>

    <code>&lt;h1&gt;Hello World&lt;/h1&gt;</code>

    <p>A basic HTML document contains several important parts:</p>

    <ul>
      <li>DOCTYPE declaration</li>
      <li>HTML element</li>
      <li>Head section</li>
      <li>Body section</li>
    </ul>

    <code>&lt;html&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</code>

  </section>


  <section class="main-section" id="CSS_Basics">
    <header>CSS Basics</header>

    <p>CSS controls the appearance and layout of HTML elements.</p>
    <p>Selectors allow developers to target specific elements on a page.</p>

    <code>body { background: white; }</code>

    <p>Common CSS properties include:</p>

    <ul>
      <li>color</li>
      <li>margin</li>
      <li>padding</li>
    </ul>

    <code>.title { font-size: 20px; }</code>

  </section>


  <section class="main-section" id="JavaScript">
    <header>JavaScript</header>

    <p>JavaScript adds interaction and dynamic behavior to websites.</p>
    <p>It can update content, respond to events, and communicate with servers.</p>

    <code>console.log("Hello World");</code>

    <p>JavaScript concepts include:</p>

    <ul>
      <li>Variables</li>
      <li>Functions</li>
      <li>Objects</li>
    </ul>

    <code>let name = "Alex";</code>

  </section>


  <section class="main-section" id="Responsive_Design">
    <header>Responsive Design</header>

    <p>Responsive design allows websites to work on different screen sizes.</p>
    <p>Media queries are commonly used to create responsive layouts.</p>

    <code>@media (max-width: 600px) { }</code>

    <p>Responsive websites often use:</p>

    <ul>
      <li>Flexible layouts</li>
      <li>Relative units</li>
      <li>Mobile-first design</li>
    </ul>

  </section>


  <section class="main-section" id="Web_Accessibility">
    <header>Web Accessibility</header>

    <p>Accessibility ensures websites can be used by everyone.</p>
    <p>Developers should consider users with different abilities.</p>

    <code>alt="Image description"</code>

    <p>Accessibility practices include:</p>

    <ul>
      <li>Using semantic HTML</li>
      <li>Providing text alternatives</li>
      <li>Supporting keyboard navigation</li>
    </ul>

  </section>


</main>

